    <h1>🩺 Horse Health</h1>
    <p>Keeping a horse healthy requires regular attention and knowing the signs of illness. Horses can hide pain well — so regular observation is key.</p>

    <h2>✅ Signs of a Healthy Horse</h2>
    <ul>
        <li>Bright, clear eyes</li>
        <li>Shiny, smooth coat</li>
        <li>Normal temperature: 37.5–38.5°C</li>
        <li>Resting heart rate: 28–44 beats per minute</li>
        <li>Breathing rate: 8–16 breaths per minute</li>
        <li>Consistent appetite and normal droppings</li>
    </ul>

    <h2>🚨 Warning Signs — When to Call the Vet</h2>
    <ul>
        <li><strong>Colic:</strong> Pawing, rolling, looking at flank — a digestive emergency</li>
        <li><strong>Lameness:</strong> Limping or refusing to bear weight on a leg</li>
        <li><strong>Fever:</strong> Temperature above 38.5°C</li>
        <li><strong>Nasal discharge:</strong> Yellow or green — sign of infection</li>
        <li><strong>Swollen legs:</strong> Could be injury or infection</li>
        <li><strong>Labored breathing:</strong> Flared nostrils at rest</li>
    </ul>

    <h2>💉 Vaccination Schedule</h2>
    <ul>
        <li><strong>Tetanus:</strong> Yearly — essential for all horses</li>
        <li><strong>Equine Influenza:</strong> Every 6–12 months</li>
        <li><strong>West Nile Virus:</strong> Annually in risk areas</li>
        <li><strong>Rabies:</strong> Annually</li>
        <li><strong>Rhinopneumonitis:</strong> Every 6 months for horses in contact with others</li>
    </ul>

    <h2>🪱 Deworming</h2>
    <ul>
        <li>Deworm every 6–12 months</li>
        <li>Rotate dewormers to prevent resistance</li>
        <li>Keep pastures clean by removing manure regularly</li>
    </ul>

    <h2>🦷 Dental Care</h2>
    <p>A veterinary dentist should float (file) the teeth every 1–2 years. Signs of dental problems: dropping food, weight loss, head tossing while riding.</p>

    <h2>🧲 Hoof Care</h2>
    <ul>
        <li>Hooves should be trimmed by a farrier every 6–8 weeks</li>
        <li>Pick hooves daily to prevent thrush</li>
        <li>Keep hooves clean and dry</li>
    </ul>

